  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\nNotable changes to the GuiKit packages (`Adliance.AspNetCore.Buddy.GuiKit`, `.Madx` and `.Infrastructure`, which are\nalways published together with the same version). Newest first.\n\n## 2026-10-26\n- Second-level navigation items in the nav have less vertical padding, to match their smaller font size.\n- Fixed the spacing of a nav item without a link that has sub-items: the next item was spaced too far from it and the\n  sub-items were indented more than below an item with a link.\n- Icons (`<i class=\"fa fa-...\">`) in nav items are as large as the item's text and all have the same width, so the\n  texts line up.\n- Fixed the spacing below a panel title when a button or link (`<agk-button>`, `<agk-link>`) follows it directly: it\n  was twice as large as before a paragraph.\n- Fixed buttons and links (`<agk-button>`, `<agk-link>`) next to each other directly in a panel, tab or `<main>`\n  (without a `<p>` around them): the whole row was pushed down by the spacing between the elements.\n\n## 2026-10-25\n- `UX-GUIDELINES.md` has new rules for the content of `<agk-title>`, when to use `<agk-breadcrumbs>`, `[From*]`\n  attributes on action method parameters and where tests go.\n\n## 2026-10-23\n- Added `<agk-breadcrumbs>` with `<agk-crumb>` children, each with a `text`, an optional `icon`, `hint` (shown muted\n  after the text) and link (`href` or `asp-*`). New CSS variables `--agk-breadcrumbs-font-size`,\n  `--agk-breadcrumbs-color-current`, `--agk-breadcrumbs-hint-color`, `--agk-breadcrumbs-separator`,\n  `--agk-breadcrumbs-separator-color` and `--agk-breadcrumbs-gap`.\n- The \"choose file\" button of `<agk-upload>` has the secondary button color instead of the primary one.\n- `<agk-button>`s and `<agk-link>`s written into `<agk-input>`, `<agk-password>` or `<agk-select>` are placed to the\n  right of the field, with the label, help text and validation message around both. They take on the field's `size`.\n- Two fieldsets (and a fieldset and a form element, button or paragraph after it) are spaced from each other anywhere,\n  eg. in a `<form>` within a tab - before, only panels and sections spaced them.\n- Links in `<agk-notification>`, in the page title and in its text (`<agk-title>`, or a `<h1>`/`<hgroup>` directly\n  in `<main>`) have the color of the surrounding text and are always underlined, instead of the link color.\n- `UX-GUIDELINES.md` is grouped by topic and has new rules for `<fieldset>` in panels and tabs, buttons inside a\n  field's tag helper, `nameof` in action links, view models and `TempData`/`ViewData`.\n\n## 2026-10-19\n- Added `<agk-tabs>`, a card (like a panel) with `<agk-tab>` children in its header, whose content is either written\n  within them or loaded via htmx the first time a tab is shown. New CSS variables `--agk-tabs-background`,\n  `--agk-tabs-font-size`, `--agk-tabs-padding-block`, `--agk-tabs-padding-inline`, `--agk-tabs-color`,\n  `--agk-tabs-color-selected`, `--agk-tabs-indicator-color`, `--agk-tabs-indicator-height` and\n  `--agk-tabs-content-padding`.\n- Fixed XSS: `<agk-title text>`, `<agk-panel title>` and `<agk-loading text>` were rendered as HTML, and the `icon` of\n  `<agk-panel>` and `<agk-notification>` wasn't encoded either - so values from a database or a user could inject\n  scripts. All of them are HTML-encoded now, like all other attributes already were.\n- **Breaking:** `<agk-title text>`, `<agk-panel title>` and `<agk-loading text>` are plain text. HTML in them is shown\n  as text, and HTML entities as they are written: replace eg. `title=\"Terms &amp; Conditions\"` with\n  `title=\"Terms & Conditions\"`. For formatted text below a page title, use the content of `<agk-title>`.\n- **Breaking:** `<agk-chart model>` doesn't accept a string with JavaScript anymore (it throws). Move the JavaScript\n  into a `<script>` child of `<agk-chart>`. Razor values in that script have to be serialized to JSON, without quotes:\n  `{ name: @Json.Serialize(Model.Name) }`, never `'@Model.Name'`.\n\n## 2026-10-13\n- Added `<agk-table>` with `<agk-table-header>`, `<agk-table-body>` and `<agk-table-footer>`: rows are highlighted on\n  hover (`hover-row`) and a click on a row follows its first link (`link-row`), both on by default. New CSS variable\n  `--agk-table-row-background-hover`.\n- Added UI/UX guidelines for views built with GuiKit (`UX-GUIDELINES.md`, shipped with the package).\n\n## 2026-10-05\n- Added `<agk-pagination>`.\n- Added `<agk-sidebar>` for a navigation on the left.\n- Buttons and pagination links show a spinner while loading.\n- Added a `confirm` attribute to delete buttons for an \"are you sure\" dialog.\n- Fixed the hover of `<agk-rating>` (and other controls based on unstyled buttons) showing the button hover background.\n\n## 2026-10-01\n- Added `<agk-password>`, an input with a toggle to show the password.\n- Buttons support different colors.\n- The MADx login layout is responsive.\n- **Breaking:** AppInsights and KeyVault extensions moved to the new package `Adliance.AspNetCore.Buddy.GuiKit.Infrastructure`\n  (referenced by GuiKit, so no new package reference is needed; change `using` directives to `Adliance.AspNetCore.Buddy.GuiKit.Infrastructure[.Extensions]`).\n\n## 2026-09-30\n- Restructured the CSS with consistent `--agk-*` variable names and cascade layers.\n- Added a common base layout `_AgkLayout`; the MADx layouts are based on it.\n- Added `<agk-button>`, `<agk-modal>`, `<agk-chart>`, `<agk-upload>`, `<agk-checkbox>` and `<agk-chat>`.\n- Selects support sizes; ratings support `readonly`; chat bubbles have a loading animation.\n- Page transitions.\n- Support for a strict CSP by default.\n- `app.UseGuiKitStaticFiles()` for proper caching of static assets.\n- Accessibility improvements and improved form and button styling.\n- The MADx package depends on the GuiKit package of the same version (published together).\n\n## 2026-09-23\n- Configuration order with Key Vault: appsettings.json, Key Vault, environment variables,\n  appsettings.{Environment}.json - so environment variables can override Key Vault secrets.\n\n## 2026-09-09\n- Added `<agk-rating>`.\n- Added `<agk-textarea>`, like `<agk-input>`.\n\n## 2026-08-20\n- `<agk-loading>` supports a `text` attribute and arbitrary HTML attributes.\n- Table header and footer have correct border radii.\n\n## 2026-08-19\n- Inputs support sizes.\n\n## 2026-08-18\n- Added `AddKeyVaultIfConfigured()`, which adds Azure Key Vault as a configuration source if a `KeyVault` connection\n  string is configured.\n- MADx: fixed text decoration of header links; adjusted margins of the login page.\n\n## 2026-08-10\n- MADx: restructured the login layout; it sets `ViewData[\"Version\"]` to the assembly version.\n- MADx: styling of ASP.NET validation errors (`.field-validation-error`).\n- The text decoration of links is configurable via a CSS variable.\n\n## 2026-08-06\n- MADx: moved the logo a little more to the top.\n\n## 2026-08-05\n- Added `<agk-select>`.\n- Form elements inside a `<fieldset>` are laid out side by side.\n- Form controls use `color-scheme: dark` for better native browser controls.\n- Fixed missing static web assets in the MADx package.\n\n## 2026-08-04\n- Added the analyzer that flags tag helper attributes set to their default value.\n- Upgraded FontAwesome to 7.3.1; its CSS is no longer bundled into `min.css` (fixes relative font paths).\n- `<agk-panel>` loads its htmx content on `load, submit` by default.\n- Fixed builds on Windows.\n\n## 2026-07-23\n- Fixed `hx-post` inside panels; it now sends a CSRF token.\n- `<agk-loading>` no longer has a text (added again on 2026-08-20).\n\n## 2026-07-22\n- More htmx settings for panels.\n\n## 2026-07-20\n- `<agk-loading>` supports a status text.\n- Improved margins of elements inside panels.\n- Added a placeholder login layout.\n\n## 2026-07-18\n- Initial version, a copy of the previous public version of GuiKit.\n- Added the MADx theme package.\n- Added `<agk-input>` and `<agk-form-element>` for reusable form elements.\n- Improved button styles.",
